7 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:18:49-07:00","id":867187,"title":"","content":"I once used Me!Me!Me! as an inspiration for my durance. The keeper had recently grown bored with her old Title, and had decided to try styling itself as an avenger of wronged women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:23:39-07:00","id":867191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867187#post867187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once used Me!Me!Me! as an inspiration for my durance. The keeper had recently grown bored with her old Title, and had decided to try styling itself as an avenger of wronged women.</div> </div> </div> </div> I prefer to think of Me!Me!Me! as an example of a True Fae using Dream Warping.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:10:12-07:00","id":867238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867191#post867191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I prefer to think of Me!Me!Me! as an example of a True Fae using Dream Warping.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's Dream Warping?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:29:33-07:00","id":867253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867238#post867238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's Dream Warping?</div> </div> </div> </div> A set of oneiromancy techniques exclusive to the True Fae in 1ED. They require a dream phial to be placed next to the dreamer, or the presence of the True Fae. These techniques use Persuasion (strange beauty) or Intimidation (pure terror) instead of the Empathy used by changelings. These dreams can Ensorcell the dreamer (i.e. give them the ability to see past the Mask), cause many derangements over months, be brutally harvested for Glamour and any other sleep-related awfulness you can imagine.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing Me!Me!Me! was a mix of Persuasion and Intimidation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:45:59-07:00","id":867266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867253#post867253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A set of oneiromancy techniques exclusive to the True Fae in 1ED. They require a dream phial to be placed next to the dreamer, or the presence of the True Fae. These techniques use Persuasion (strange beauty) or Intimidation (pure terror) instead of the Empathy used by changelings. These dreams can Ensorcell the dreamer (i.e. give them the ability to see past the Mask), cause many derangements over months, be brutally harvested for Glamour and any other sleep-related awfulness you can imagine.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing Me!Me!Me! was a mix of Persuasion and Intimidation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, in English, it's screwing with people's heads by invading and controlling their dreams, but in a more powerful form than Changelings have access to?<br /> <br /> <br /> The description sort of reminds me of Luke telling Percy how Cronos gave him horrible nightmares to punish him for losing the Master Bolt in &quot;Percy Jackson and the Lightning Thief&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. I'd put Me!Me!Me! as Intimidation. The not-scary opening part just serves to add emotional whiplash to the rest of the dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:58:34-07:00","id":867279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867266#post867266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, in English, it's screwing with people's heads by invading and controlling their dreams, but in a more powerful form than Changelings have access to?<br /> <br /> <br /> The description sort of reminds me of Luke telling Percy how Cronos gave him horrible nightmares to punish him for losing the Master Bolt in &quot;Percy Jackson and the Lightning Thief&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. I'd put Me!Me!Me! as Intimidation. The not-scary opening part just serves to add emotional whiplash to the rest of the dream.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's basically it, yeah. Furthermore, the True Fae don't need Pledges or Contracts to use Dream Warping. It is not just a matter of power, but also consent and privacy.<br /> <br /> What part of my post was too complicated? I was just using the game's terminology. I assumed you had the 1ED Core Rulebook. Sorry if that's not the case.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, Me!Me!Me! is probably Intimidation. It is only alluring in the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:58:05-07:00","id":867306,"title":"","content":"I also don't typically use the <i>&quot;bad touch, bad touch, I need an adult&quot;</i> style Durance unless I plan to make a Keeper into a sinister monster. I like the idea of a durance being both wondrous as well as dangerous. Arcadia should be a place that, if you could look past its faults, would be a fantastic place to live. Which only further adds to the danger that the Keepers pose upon the Lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> You catch more flies with honey.<br /> <br /> <br /> A happy worker is a hard worker.<br /> <br /> <br /> The best slave is one who serves willingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> platitudes, platitudes, est.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T20:45:50-07:00","id":867335,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, would the Dark Souls series be an appropriate Durance, considering the series is stuck in a recurring time loop of the world going to shit? The hero fights through waves of &quot;fuck you&quot; strong enemies and at the end of it all, gets to decide whether to keep the time loop going, or break the cycle and let the world finally end?<br /> <br /> And the fact that many of those boss monsters were once people who underwent the same trial and choose to perpetuate the time loop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T21:13:01-07:00","id":867350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867306#post867306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't typically use the <i>&amp;quot;bad touch, bad touch, I need an adult&amp;quot;</i> style Durance unless I plan to make a Keeper into a sinister monster. I like the idea of a durance being both wondrous as well as dangerous. Arcadia should be a place that, if you could look past its faults, would be a fantastic place to live. Which only further adds to the danger that the Keepers pose upon the Lost.<br /> <br /> You catch more flies with honey.<br /> <br /> A happy worker is a hard worker.<br /> <br /> The best slave is one who serves willingly.<br /> <br /> platitudes, platitudes, est.</div> </div> </div> </div> Words of wisdom, right here. I won't deny that Durances involving heavy subjects happen, but I just find them more interesting when the associated emotions aren't exactly clear cut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867335#post867335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, would the Dark Souls series be an appropriate Durance, considering the series is stuck in a recurring time loop of the world going to shit? The hero fights through waves of &amp;quot;fuck you&amp;quot; strong enemies and at the end of it all, gets to decide whether to keep the time loop going, or break the cycle and let the world finally end?<br /> <br /> And the fact that many of those boss monsters were once people who underwent the same trial and choose to perpetuate the time loop?</div> </div> </div> </div> I consider Dark Souls as closer to Promethean, what with the juxtaposition between despair and hope, searching for the guidance of other undead, trying to not go Hollow/Centimanus and the fair amount of body horror.<br /> <br /> But if you wanted to use it as inspiration for Changeling, I'd say you shouldn't limit it to a Durance. Set the Chronicle or parts of it around a horrible curse looming over the Freehold. Abnormal incursions from the Hedge become more frequent, threatening the Bulwark. The Clarity and lives of the changelings are at stake. The Courts of Dusk and Dawn get more members and visibility, but the former eventually prepares them for the final stand. The players should keep asking themselves &quot;are we going to make it?&quot; and &quot;is it even worth trying?&quot;. The story of Dark Souls is very much in line with the Dusk Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T21:44:11-07:00","id":867367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867350#post867350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Words of wisdom, right here. I won't deny that Durances involving heavy subjects happen, but I just find them more interesting when the associated emotions aren't exactly clear cut.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, like the story of a jealous Queen who rules over a land of magic and fantasy. The lands are prosperous, the environment is beautiful and the mines never seem to run dry of precious resources. Now sure, there's a strict no tolerance policy on Fairest Kiths in the kingdom. Just don't have the audacity to challenge the Queen's looks or authority and we don't have a problem! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-18-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T00:34:35-07:00","id":867412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845008-what-are-durances-usually-like-in-your-games?p=867279#post867279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's basically it, yeah. Furthermore, the True Fae don't need Pledges or Contracts to use Dream Warping. It is not just a matter of power, but also consent and privacy.<br /> <br /> What part of my post was too complicated? I was just using the game's terminology. I assumed you had the 1ED Core Rulebook. Sorry if that's not the case.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, Me!Me!Me! is probably Intimidation. It is only alluring in the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ok. I do have a PDF of it, but it's been a while since i was in an actual game, so I'm rusty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}